# Windows stack & data flow — "Lenovo Fn and function keys" 2.0.0.25

Package: `10-extracted/code$getextractpath$/source/` (Inno-Setup payload of
`01lf0aafar2w6jb0.exe`, sha256 3e30c034…cf7b6d). DriverVer 04/25/2022,2.0.0.25.
Class = System, Provider = Lenovo. **User-mode package only — no kernel-mode .sys.**

## 1. Installation / binding

| Item | Value | Source |
|---|---|---|
| INF | `LenovoFnAndFunctionKeys.inf` (UTF-16) | source/lenovofnandfunctionkeys.inf |
| Class / GUID | `System` / `{4d36e97d-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}` | inf:7-8 |
| CatalogFile | `LenovoFnAndFunctionKeys.cat` | inf:10 |
| Hardware ID | `ACPI\LHK2019` → `LnvHsaDevice_Install` | inf:17-18 |
| Service | `LenovoFnAndFunctionKeys`, `ServiceType=0x10` (OWN_PROCESS), `StartType=2` (AUTO), `ErrorControl=0` | inf ([LnvHsa_Service]) |
| ServiceBinary | `%13%\LenovoUtilityService.exe` → `C:\Windows\System32\drivers\LenovoUtilityService.exe` (`13`=`DestinationDirs` drivers dir, `DefaultDestDir=13`) | inf [LnvHsaService_Files]/[DestinationDirs] |
| Kernel driver | **NONE** | see §4 |

`ACPI\LHK2019` is DSDT `Device (HKDV)` (`20-acpi/dsl/DSDT.dsl:24670`), an *empty* device
(only `_STA`). The INF's only job is to make Windows install+start the user-mode service
when the firmware exposes LHK2019.

### dpinst.xml / dpinst.exe
`dpinst.xml` (34 KB) is a **generic DPInst wizard config**: a single `<search><subDirectory>*`
rule plus ~30 localized `<language>` blocks whose titles are the template string
"Energy Management Driver" and `<finishText>` boilerplate. It contains **no driver logic,
no INF list, no flags**. `dpinst.exe` is the stock Microsoft Driver Package Installer whose
embedded watermark is `dpinstwatermark.bmp`. Nothing here affects the camera/blur feature.

### lenovofnandfunctionkeys.cat (signature)
PKCS#7 SignedData (DER) security catalog. Raw DER (`cat:raw`) yields:
- `HWID1acpi\lhk2019`, `Qualification Level 10000`, `Submission ID 29997810_…`,
  `BundleID 23bac19b-6555-446b-a615-513c12e495b6`, `OSAttr 2:10.00`, `Universal False`, `Declarative True`.
- Catalog **member files** (hash entries): `mmstate.dll`, `ludp.dll`, `blurswitchcs.dll`,
  `intelcontrollib.dll`, `msvcp140.dll`, `controllib.dll`, `vcruntime140.dll`,
  `vcruntime140_1.dll`, `atiadlxx.dll`, `lenovo.assemblyvalidation.native.dll`,
  `fnhotkeyutility.exe`, `ludp.net.dll`, `qrcode.png`, `qrcode.html`,
  `lenovofnandfunctionkeys.inf`, `lenovoutilityservice.exe`. **No `.sys`.**
- Signer chain: leaf `Microsoft Windows Hardware Compatibility Publisher`
  (issuer `Microsoft Windows Third Party Component CA 2012`, validity 2021-06-17→2022-06-16)
  → `Microsoft Root Certificate Authority 2010`; RFC3161 countersignature by
  `Microsoft Time-Stamp PCA 2010` (2022-04-26).

Verify on a machine with openssl (equivalent to the brief's command):
`openssl pkcs7 -inform DER -print_certs -in lenovofnandfunctionkeys.cat`
(openssl could not be executed by this agent — read-only toolset; the above is read from the raw DER).

